<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olous</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Olus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Olous was an ancient Greek city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mirabello">Gulf of Mirabello</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, near modern Elounda. Its remains now lie partly under the sea because of the sinking of the coast. Inscriptions record its treaties and conflicts with Lato and its ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a>, and it had a famous wooden statue of Britomartis said to be the work of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daedalus">Daedalus</a>.</p></div>
